          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How an order works</h2>
          <p>
            Every order follows the same four steps, from the customer's table
            to the cashier.
          </p>

          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Step</th>
                  <th>Who</th>
                  <th>What happens</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>1. Take the order</td>
                  <td>Waiter</td>
                  <td>Writes down what the customer wants</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>2. Cook the food</td>
                  <td>Chef</td>
                  <td>Prepares the order in the kitchen</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>3. Serve the table</td>
                  <td>Waiter</td>
                  <td>Brings the food and drinks to the table</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>4. Take the payment</td>
                  <td>Cashier</td>
                  <td>Prints the bill and receives the money</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="note">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> always repeat the order to the customer
            before you send it to the kitchen, so there are no mistakes.
          </div>
        </section>
